WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.700
Listen to us!

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.460
Just release Tashiro—

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.300
What is this?

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.690
Is it coming from those scribbles?

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.630
Girls... Die.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.490
Girls... Die...

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.630
<b>Eleventh Haunting 
The Worst Possible Meeting</b>

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.100
Die.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.920
Girls... Die.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.260
Girls! Die!

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.170
Stop it!

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.510
Y-You okay, Tashiro?

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.540
Yeah... You?

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.150
I'm fine.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.620
Ow...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.740
Miura's gone.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.090
Looks like he ran off.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.420
What's with that guy?

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.870
He was incredibly strong!

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.170
I went flying. That should be impossible!

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.090
Right...

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.150
And did he just throw a student?

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.720
Now I'm mad!

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.880
Calm down...

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.910
<i>But she's right. This doesn't make sense.</i>

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.370
<i>Where's Miura getting that power?</i>

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:54.840
<i>And those black bug-like things 
seemed to possess him.</i>

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.890
Tashiro? What's wrong?

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.400
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.380
I've decided...

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:08.050
If that's how he wants it, I'll learn 
all there is to know about him.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.200
I'll use my network of online friends 
to discover exactly who he is.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.710
Bye!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.060
Girls are strong.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.290
Truly...

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.200
Fool!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.160
Where the hell were you?

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.530
That was spooky back there, yes?

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:29.180
Why didn't you tell me when Miura arrived?!

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.980
That isn't fair, master...

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.110
I don't even want to sense the 
auras of such lowly creatures.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.240
The one area where you have pride, huh?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.560
Human auras are tainted things.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.070
And my delicate heart only 
detects beautiful, pure auras.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.290
Fine, fine...

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.160
Norns!

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.670
Did you call us, master?

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.270
What manga did they read this time?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.020
Master?

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.840
Can you look into what happened back there?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.370
Curious?

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.380
Yeah. I want to know about that black thing.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:14.950
What's wrong?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.320
It's gone.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.530
That muddy thing is gone from the room.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.350
Gone?

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.760
That's impossible. I just saw it.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.950
Are there yokai that can just 
appear and disappear?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.550
That is impossible.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:35.600
Ghosts and yokai are not so indistinct.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.160
They appear in forms that we can sense.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.810
So it wasn't a ghost or yokai?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.640
Can you tell me more, Norns?

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.880
Sorry.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.030
Why not ask Cait Sith—

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.820
You still believe in that liar cat, Urdr?!

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.310
But...

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.540
Stop it!

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.010
How many times has that cat tricked you?

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.010
Who else knows things?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.900
Him... Chokmah!

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.860
Do you need something?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.970
Can you think of something muddy

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:14.290
and stuck in one place, 
which isn't a yokai or ghost?

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.610
That's, well...

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.330
It could be many things.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:26.560
A portal to the demon world

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.890
from which negative energy 
flows outward, perhaps.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:30.920
The demon world?

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.980
If that were true, we'd have 
big problems right now!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.890
The demon world's miasma instantly
 transforms a person into a monster.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:44.310
And a hole to the demon world 
doesn't simply open, anyway.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.090
What else could it be?

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.740
Memories, perhaps?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.450
Memories?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.160
Yes, the memories of a thing!

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.300
In an old castle was a room 
called the "slaughter room."

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:05.510
When a lord caught his wife 
in bed with another man,

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.960
he slew both of them there.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.420
Even decades later, they would appear,

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:18.660
writhing and covered in blood.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:24.570
Due to their powerful emotional states at 
the time when they suffered and died,

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.300
which were burnt into the room.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.190
Powerful emotions...

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:37.620
Old man, could the feelings doing that 
be hatred or the desire to curse others?

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.560
Indeed.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.750
The emotions remain.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.610
Strong sorrow, hatred, and terror.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:50.970
Emotions that easily accrue can 
build up in a single place.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:56.320
Even if their originator forgets or vanishes,

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:00.360
the emotions persist there.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.700
Emotions that persist, 
even if their originator forgets.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.070
Sounds like the id...

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.020
The id?

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:12.420
That which knows not good or evil, loss or 
gain, contradiction, time, or space,

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:16.130
existing only to fulfill the demands 
of the unconscious.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.830
That's what I read in a book.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.160
That's...

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.030
It was in a movie Hase and I saw as kids.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.960
The protagonist's evil desires

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.420
took the form of a monster of the id.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.860
The misogyny of whoever scribbled those words

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.400
accumulated in that place.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.750
That was a monster of the id.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.280
But it's gone now.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.690
Old man, can that id monster wander around?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:55.560
Those things desire a vessel 
more than anything.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:56.950
A vessel?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.880
A large amount of emotion 
is a powerful being.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:04.880
Sometimes, it begins to 
seek a body for itself.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:09.120
And any vessel will do, 
whether thing or person.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.000
You have heard many stories about 
dolls with souls, haven't you?

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:18.420
The formless seek to enter form.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:26.770
That which is empty makes 
an especially good vessel.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.690
<b>Faculty Room</b>

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.530
Yes, thank you.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.940
And about this part...

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.330
Sensei? Miura-sensei?

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.230
I brought the plan for the 
Drama Club's activities.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.010
Thanks...

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.540
Are you okay?

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:15.910
Sorry, I've just got a headache.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.240
Shouldn't you go to the nurse's office?

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.120
No, I'm fine.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.080
What's their problem?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.280
Do they think they can tell us what to do?

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.460
Let's teach them a lesson.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.730
Are you okay, Sensei?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.540
Sensei...

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.310
Miura?

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.450
Get back!

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:08.030
<i>He looks so worn-down...</i>

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.420
<i>It's only been a few days 
since he first went crazy.</i>

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.970
<i>Is he really possessed by an id monster?</i>

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.460
<i>What happened in his past?</i>

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.770
What would you like to do, master?

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:44.410
<i>The minute I start training as a mage, 
running into a heavy case like this...</i>

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:48.220
Don't get involved in any weird stuff.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.780
<i>Hase...</i>

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.840
<i>I'm sorry,</i>

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:58.420
<i>but I want to solve the 
mysteries of this case.</i>

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.670
<i>And the meaning of our encounter.</i>

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.720
So Miura-sensei saw the girl and collapsed?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:30.220
These misogynistic emotions are 
possessing him at irregular intervals?

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.820
I think so, too.

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:34.020
You do?

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.360
I don't know what to do.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:40.850
Oh? Thinking of an exorcism, 
now that you're a master mage?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:42.470
That isn't it!

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.860
I just want a specialist's opinion.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:48.150
But Ryu-san and Furuhonya-san are both out.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:52.350
And Akine-chan is off on 
some kind of school trip.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:56.300
At a time like this, 
why can't I reach anyone?

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.200
Well, that's a problem...

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:04.140
But even if he is possessed, 
performing an exorcism would be difficult.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.750
You'd need his or his family's permission.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:12.270
To his family, knowing none of this,

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:15.750
he doesn't need an exorcism 
but medical treatment.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.100
Even if that won't work.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.880
Right...

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.380
That's right.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.590
Even if Akine-chan were here,

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.420
we can't just break into his room 
and perform an exorcism.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.640
If we did that, we'd be the 
ones sent to the hospital.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.990
That's how the world works.

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:36.770
Strange, huh?

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:40.230
It used to be worse.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:43.450
People who collapsed from 
minor mental problems

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.910
were said to be "fox-possessed."

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.690
And people thought violence 
would drive the fox out,

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:52.470
so they'd beat them en masse 
or imprison them forever.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:56.980
Sometimes, the whole family 
would be considered cursed.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.350
In the end,

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:03.480
discrimination and fear toward 
the unknown doesn't change.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.910
Can't be helped, though.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.560
Sato-san?

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:11.030
That's the way I was before I died...

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.550
Mariko-san?

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:15.140
Looks, trends...

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.340
I just followed them, 
not thinking about a thing.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.780
I feared what was different

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.590
and discriminated against it.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.640
Basically, I was an idiot.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.090
So,

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.250
studying is really important, Yushi-kun!

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.120
See, hear, and read a lot,

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.910
and expand your world!

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.450
R-Right...

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:40.400
That's Mariko-chan for you! Smart thinking!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.120
I've been dead for a few decades, 
and I've spent them thinking!

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.040
Anyway, back to drinking!

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.270
<i>Their words were very heavy.</i>

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.850
<i>They'd probably seen that 
many times in their lives.</i>

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:56.390
Well,

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.310
it's hard to tell a person who's alive

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.000
to seriously study ghosts and yokai.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.860
That's right!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.330
Even though they're making movies like that.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.200
Oh! It's so scary!

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:10.720
<i>Jeez...</i>

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.470
<i>I don't know what to do.</i>

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.120
<i>And I'm so close. It's frustrating.</i>

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.090
<i>But maybe Sato-san's right.</i>

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:22.040
<i>Maybe all I can do now is watch.</i>

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.250
<i>Me? Save Miura?</i>

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.160
<i>That's ridiculous—</i>

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:28.940
Kuri?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.760
Thanks.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.420
It's good!

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.980
This croquette is great!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.890
The potatoes and ground beef...

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.720
It's so simple, but the taste is so complex.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:44.180
Packed, but so light on the tongue!

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.670
And it's so sweet...

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:53.430
Today's snack was Ruriruri's 
potato croquettes, huh?

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.460
It's cold, but the crust is crispy.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.730
And the salt and pepper are perfect.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.530
That's Ruriko's magic for you.

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:00.820
It is magic!

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:04.170
And when you want a midnight snack...

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.920
A midnight snack?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.830
You can warm it in the microwave,

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.100
put it on cold rice,

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.170
top with some sauce,

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.850
then add yellow radish!

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.130
It's amazing!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:21.230
Warm in the microwave 
and put it on cold rice?

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.720
Warm in the microwave 
and put it on cold rice!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.120
O-Oh, wow...

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.260
Ruriko-san, do you have any croquettes left?!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:35.580
What about cold rice? And yellow radish?

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:36.540
For me, too!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.450
And me!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.710
I put my croquettes on soba noodles, chirp.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.360
You do what, chirp?

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.890
I mix them with eggs, chirp.

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:45.500
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:49.680
Hello!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.960
This is the Yokai Ap— I mean Kotobuki-so.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.030
This looks so good.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.780
Just a second.

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:57.260
Is not waiting for others okay?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.360
Yushi-kun! Call from Tashiro-chan!

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.360
Don't tell the others.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:00.430
Tashiro?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.580
Hey, Inaba...

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:02.990
Get a cell phone!

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.680
Talking to other people makes me nervous!

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.440
How did you get the number for this place?

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.240
<i>It doesn't matter, does it?</i>

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>Anyway, I heard Miura collapsed?</i>

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.740
Yeah.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.300
<i>I see. I discovered a lot, too.</i>

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:18.160
<i>Like what happened at his old school.</i>

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.400
Really? And?

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.460
I got a photo, as well.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.410
He looks like a totally different person!

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:25.350
Want to see it?

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:26.540
<i>Y-Yeah.</i>

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.640
<i>Right?</i>

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.350
<i>Then, come to the front door.</i>

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:34.380
Don't tell me...

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.090
Tash—

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.380
Hey, there! I came by!

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:40.580
Listen...

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.890
If our sexes were swapped, I'd call the cops!

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.280
This place is really retro, huh?

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.070
How did you find this place?!

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:51.440
I do whatever it takes to get information.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.340
Especially private information 
on my classmates...

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.790
Who's that?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.860
Do you want to be in the CIA?

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.300
Maybe...

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.130
Forget it.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:06.160
Then, what's this about Miura?

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.830
Oh, right.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.220
Look at this, first.

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:12.970
It's a photo taken when Miura 
first became a teacher.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.220
<b>English   Katsumasa Miura</b>

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.990
He really does look like a different person!

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.480
It was just a few years ago, right?

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:22.700
Look at the title of the album.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.770
<b>Twelfth 
Shiramine Girls' High School 
Graduation Album</b>

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.770
Shiramine Girls' High?

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.630
A girls' high school?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.040
Shiramine is a hard school to get into,

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:32.260
and it's got a good reputation.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.410
All its clubs and teams are well respected.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.890
The Drama Club, specifically, 
wins lots of competitions each year.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.830
So wasn't that good for Miura?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:45.210
It's just that girls there can be nasty.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.540
Nasty?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.710
<b>Takanodai Central Hospital</b>

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.360
There are many rumors.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:52.230
They're good, but also very proud.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:55.700
And they ignore newer teachers.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.050
That's...

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:02.370
Last year, Miura supposedly 
quit for personal reasons.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.850
But the real cause was a fight 
with the Drama Club girls

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.870
that ended with something 
terrible happening to him

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:10.560
and his refusal to go to school.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.230
Something terrible?

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:15.400
Something that totally changed 
his appearance.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:20.290
And after a two-year recovery, 
he came to JTB.

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:24.620
Looks like he's totally dragged it 
with him, instead of getting better.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.210
So that's why girls have to die, huh?

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.530
<i>Miura suffered at the hands of girls.</i>

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.160
<i>His pride and self-confidence were ruined.</i>

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.110
<i>When he came to JTB, he was an empty shell.</i>

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:43.590
<i>A room filled with the hatred an 
unknown person had for women.</i>

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:47.600
<i>Miura, the Drama Club adviser, 
would inevitably go there.</i>

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.480
<i>Miura, emptied out because of girls...</i>

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:07.610
<i>The id monster, waiting for a vessel.</i>

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:11.340
<i>It was the worst possible</i>

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:14.620
<i>encounter of fate.</i>

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:26.240
What's wrong, Inaba?

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.120
Nothing.

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.760
<i>They have to suffer.</i>

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.630
I have a bike.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.710
You don't need to walk me back!

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.390
Yeah, I do.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.880
<i>Now I know how the id monster and Miura met.</i>

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.910
<i>But something still doesn't feel right.</i>

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.320
<i>What is it?</i>

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.830
Come to think of it,

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:18.660
why do you have this photo 
in your student notebook?

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.440
<b>Double Peace 

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.870
When did you get that?! Is that 
how you found my address?

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.690
Is that your girlfriend?

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:27.430
Are you stupid?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:28.520
He's a guy!

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.610
You take photos like that with other guys?

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:34.400
You girls do it all the time!

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.700
But it's different, isn't it?

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:40.700
<i>Anyway, the id monster wanted a vessel.</i>

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:44.590
<i>Because it wanted to go 
someplace to do something.</i>

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:48.720
<i>It felt like the first thing it'd 
done was pursue Tashiro...</i>

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:51.730
<i>for some reason.</i>

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.400
This is it! This is the place!

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.270
I'll lock up my bike.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.310
Okay.

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.840
<i>But Miura collapsed just this afternoon...</i>

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.190
<i>It might be too soon.</i>

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:09.170
Tashiro!

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:16.410
Are you okay—

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.730
Tashiro!

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:12.850
An id monster?

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:14.990
I can't believe something like that exists...

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:16.120
What do I do?

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:17.620
It's my turn.

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:18.490
Akine-san?

00:23:18.490 --> 00:23:20.670
Bring it on, id thing!

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:23.260
I'll show you the results of my training.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:26.710
Master, I'll do my best!

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.210
It's like something's flipped her switch.

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:31.640
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:33.080
I'm Going to the Future.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:33.300
<b>Twelfth Haunting 
I'm Going to the Future</b>

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:34.310
I want to do something.

00:23:34.310 --> 00:23:36.250
If this is my fate...
